  V3  THE HONEST STATEMENT: THE SHAPE-LOCK IS PARTIALLY-CONFIRMED.
        - The MW outer slope sits ON its locked gamma under BOTH anchors:
          vs the deep RAR reading's n=1.20 (locked 2.67) z = -0.92, vs the
          phantom class n=2 (locked 2.00) z = +0.75.  The MW-20-100 channel
          does not contradict the lock; it interpolates the two anchors.
        - The cluster inner -1.53 is ON the gamma locked by the RECONCILED
          n*=3.16 (locked 1.63, z = -0.41) and OFF the phantom n=2 (z = -1.88):
          the lock does not force the phantom there -- the composite selects n.
        - The dust envelope -2.38 is OFF the ALT-deep-end anchor n=1.66
          (locked 2.20, z = +1.17, marginal) and ON its own selected n=1.45:
          an effective-window channel where the per-cluster spread dominates.
        - The cluster residual -1.478 is OFF the phantom class n=2 (z=-2.09)
          and ON the reconciled n*=3.16 (z=-0.62): G008's own message -- the
          baryon-steepened isothermal is NOT the pure phantom; the composite
          and the reconciled n* carry it.
        BOTTOM LINE, WITH THE NUMBERS: 3/4 primary/secondary readings sit on a
        committed locked gamma at |z| <= 1 (MW 0.92, cluster vs n* 0.41,
